    {
      "id": 1,
      "stage": 1,
      "type": "reading_card",
      "title": "Colors in Korean",
      "title_kr": "색깔",
      "body": "Korean has two ways to express colors. Descriptive adjectives end in -다 (e.g., 빨갛다 = to be red) and are used in sentences. Color nouns end in -색 (color) and are used to name the color itself. Both forms are widely used.",
      "tip": {
        "icon": "🎨",
        "label": "-색 vs. adjective form",
        "text": "빨간색 (the color red) vs. 빨개요 (it is red). For naming a color outright, use the -색 form. For describing something, use the adjective form: 이 셔츠는 빨개요 (This shirt is red)."
      },
      "body_ja": "韓国語で色を表現するには2つの方法があります。-다で終わる形容詞（例：빨갛다＝赤い）は文中で使い、-색（色）で終わる名詞は色そのものを指します。両方広く使われます。",
      "tip_ja": {
        "label": "-색 vs. 形容詞形",
        "text": "빨간색（赤という色）vs. 빨개요（赤いです）。色そのものを指すときは-색形を、何かを描写するときは形容詞形を使います：이 셔츠는 빨개요（このシャツは赤い）。"
      }
    },
